## 5. Non-Functional Testing

### 5.1 Performance Considerations

| Metric | Target | Measurement |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| Recording start time | < 3 seconds | Time from click to recording |
| Memory usage | < 500MB | Chrome task manager during recording |
| CPU usage | < 30% | During HD recording |
| File size accuracy | 1 Mbps (SD) / 2.5 Mbps (HD) | Bytes / duration |

### 5.2 Reliability and Stability

| Scenario | Expected Behavior |
|----------|-------------------|
| 30-minute recording | Completes without crash |
| Rapid start/stop cycles | State remains consistent |
| Popup open/close 50 times | No memory leak |
| Service worker termination | Self-heals, recording continues |

### 5.3 Error Handling and Recovery

| Error Scenario | Expected Recovery |
|----------------|-------------------|
| Permission denied | Returns to IDLE, no error lingering |
| Offscreen document crash | Error shown, state reset to IDLE |
| IndexedDB quota exceeded | Error shown, partial save if possible |
| Chrome crash during recording | Data lost (expected limitation) |

### 5.4 Logging and Observability

| Log Type | Location | Content |
|----------|----------|---------|
| FSM transitions | Service worker console | State changes with reasons |
| Message routing | Service worker console | Message types received |
| Offscreen events | Offscreen console | MediaRecorder events |
| Content script | Page console | Floating pane lifecycle |

---

## 6. Traceability Matrix

### 6.1 Feature to Test Case Mapping

| Feature | Test Cases |
|---------|------------|
| FR-001: Start Recording | TC-001, TC-002, TC-003, TC-004, TC-025 |
| FR-002: Stop Recording | TC-005, TC-006, TC-007, TC-026 |
| FR-003: External Stop | TC-008, TC-009 |
| FR-004: Pause Recording | TC-010, TC-027 |
| FR-005: Resume Recording | TC-010, TC-011, TC-012, TC-013 |
| FR-006: Video Quality | TC-014, TC-015 |
| FR-007: Capture Mode | TC-001, TC-002 |
| FR-008: Floating Pane | TC-006, TC-016, TC-017, TC-018 |
| FR-009: Size Limits | TC-021, TC-022 |
| FR-010: State Persistence | TC-019, TC-020 |

### 6.2 High-Risk Areas Requiring Deeper Coverage

| Area | Risk Level | Reason | Recommended Tests |
|------|------------|--------|-------------------|
| FSM Transitions | High | Core state management | All state transitions |
| External Stop | High | Edge case, data loss risk | TC-008, TC-009, TC-012 |
| Pause Timing | Medium | Duration calculation | TC-010, TC-013 |
| State Persistence | Medium | Service worker lifecycle | TC-019, TC-020 |
| Content Script Injection | Medium | Dynamic injection | TC-018 |

### 6.3 Test Prioritization

**P0 (Must Pass - Release Blockers):**
- TC-001: Basic Tab Recording Start
- TC-005: Basic Stop via Popup
- TC-006: Stop via Floating Pane
- TC-008: Stop Sharing Button
- TC-010: Basic Pause and Resume
- TC-019: Close and Reopen Popup

**P1 (Should Pass):**
- TC-002, TC-003, TC-004, TC-009, TC-011, TC-012, TC-014, TC-015, TC-016, TC-017, TC-020

**P2 (Nice to Have):**
- TC-007, TC-013, TC-018, TC-021, TC-022, TC-023, TC-024, TC-025

**P3 (Low Priority):**
- TC-026, TC-027

